# HOTFIX-006A — Runtime User-Agent Experiment Report

## Executive Summary
Per your instructions, a runtime experiment was conducted to validate whether stripping `QtWebEngine/6.11.1` from the HTTP User-Agent string enables Claude.ai's Google OAuth flow.

No permanent code changes were made to the codebase.

---

## 1. Experiment Setup & Execution

1. **User-Agent Configuration**:
   - Original UA: `Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) QtWebEngine/6.11.1 Chrome/140.0.0.0 Safari/537.36`
   - Experiment UA: `Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/140.0.0.0 Safari/537.36`
   - Only `QtWebEngine/6.11.1` token was removed. Chrome version, Windows version, Safari token, and AppleWebKit token were preserved.

2. **Execution & Event Monitoring**:
   - `https://claude.ai/login` loaded cleanly under the overridden User-Agent.
   - Click event triggered on "Continue with Google" button.
   - Captured JS console, window creation events (`createWindow`), navigation requests, and GSI/FedCM status.

